# Architecture Document: On-Device Privacy-Preserving Transaction SMS Parser

## 1. Executive Summary & System Overview

### 1.1 Executive Summary
The **On-Device Privacy-Preserving Transaction SMS Parser SDK** is a production-grade, privacy-first mobile software development kit (SDK) designed for digital micro-lending fintech applications and Non-Banking Financial Companies (NBFCs) operating in India. 

Over 60% of India's Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) are excluded from formal credit markets due to a lack of traditional credit bureau footprints (thin-file borrowers). However, these merchants generate a highly dense, real-time digital footprint through Unified Payments Interface (UPI) notification SMS, bank alerts, and utility bills. 

This system solves the credit underwriting gap by parsing unstructured transaction SMS data **locally on the borrower's Android device**. It constructs an ultra-precise, real-time cash flow profile (including monthly income, average daily balance, and debt-to-income ratios) without transmitting any raw SMS text or personally identifiable information (PII) to the cloud. The SDK uploads only high-level, anonymized financial features to the lender's server.

